# LoPAS Integrated Runtime Patch

This patch connects the existing stage-local implementations without replacing
their rules.

## Added

- `src/foundry/`: Ingest → Proxy → Protocol → Simulation → Selection → Routing
  orchestration with one run manifest;
- `src/execution/`: promotion-aware, no-side-effect Shadow compiler and gate;
- execution plan, action receipt, and adapter manifest schemas;
- one-command optional continuation from Foundry to Action Receipt;
- deterministic tests for orchestration and execution gating;
- local runtime documentation and example binding/input files;
- a schema-valid synthetic Level 3 fixture that must reach `READY` without side effects.

## Install

From this patch directory:

```bash
python apply_patch.py /path/to/lopas-protocol-foundry
```

The installer refuses to overwrite changed files unless `--force` is supplied
and creates `pyproject.toml.runtime-patch.bak` before changing the package list.
Use `--dry-run` to inspect the operation.

## Test

From the repository root after installation:

```bash
python -m compileall -q src tests
python -m unittest \
  tests.test_execution_gate \
  tests.test_execution_pipeline \
  tests.test_foundry_pipeline -v
```

The patch deliberately does not add a live adapter executor. `READY` means that
a plan may be observed in shadow mode; it does not authorize an external side
effect.
